# Everything in this repo is read by bash (hooks, installer) or by Claude Code
# itself, on Linux containers and on Windows Git Bash alike. A Windows clone
# with core.autocrlf=true checks .sh files out as CRLF, which breaks the
# shebang and leaves a stray \r on the end of every unquoted value -- a failure
# that is hard to see and easy to misread as a logic bug. Pin LF in the working
# tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
